      <div class="article__main">
        <div class="article__body prose">
          <blockquote>
<ul>
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> GTA 6 targets <strong>30 FPS</strong> (30 pictures per second) on PS5, PS5 Pro and Xbox Series X|S. <strong>No 60 FPS or performance mode is announced.</strong></li>
<li><strong>PS5 Pro adds two things:</strong> <strong>PSSR</strong> (a sharper picture) and <strong>ray-traced shadows</strong> (more realistic shadows). Both are PS5 Pro only.</li>
<li><strong>Set up now:</strong> keep <strong>212 GB+</strong> free, run <strong>HDR setup</strong>, and use <strong>Game Mode</strong> on your TV. In-game options are <strong>not announced</strong>. We will update this page after launch.</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Words used on this page.</strong> <em>FPS</em> means frames per second, how smooth the picture is. <em>HDR</em> means brighter lights and deeper darks on your TV. <em>Haptics</em> means the controller buzzing to match the action.</p>
